title: "Coreward: Portable Promotion Primitives for Agent-Written Code"
message: >-
  If you use Coreward in research or engineering work, please cite
  this software using the metadata in this file (and the white paper when
  discussing mechanisms).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Coreward contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/afelin/coreward"
repository-code: "https://github.com/afelin/coreward"
url: "https://github.com/afelin/coreward"
abstract: >-
  Free open-source promotion-gate primitives for AI-assisted software change:
  authorize_write, Coreward Mode, TaskBond, Mandates, Ward, AgentId, zero-token
  gates, depth dial, forever loop, tamper-evident capsules and HPURL proof links,
  deterministic replay, adversarial gauntlet, MCP rulebook tools, local lessons
  as IP, light heal/Pearl operators, and Assisted-by attribution.
  Regulation-agnostic; posture packs are house-rule overlays, not law.
  CyberReady remains Planned when not installed (fail-open).
keywords:
  - software engineering
  - AI agents
  - promotion gates
  - reproducible evidence
  - open source
